# WhiteBox AI — environment configuration
#
# Email + password auth works out of the box (backed by a local SQLite DB at
# data/whitebox.db — no config needed).
#
# To enable REAL third-party sign-in, register an OAuth app with each provider,
# set the values below, and deploy on a host with outbound network access.
# (This dev machine blocks external HTTPS, so OAuth handshakes can't complete here.)

# Google — https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorized redirect URI: <origin>/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# GitHub — https://github.com/settings/developers
# Authorization callback URL: <origin>/api/auth/oauth/github/callback
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Microsoft — https://portal.azure.com (App registrations)
# Redirect URI: <origin>/api/auth/oauth/microsoft/callback
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
